# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Gothenburg urban digital twin prototype
# =============================================================================
#
# POLICY (see docs/decisions/2026-08-26_unity-version-control-policy.md)
#
#   Git tracks SOURCE only: Python pipeline code, Unity C# scripts, Unity
#   project/package settings, configs, docs, tests.
#
#   Git NEVER tracks DATA: nothing under Raw_data/ or Processed_data/, no
#   meshes, point clouds, rasters, or generated scene geometry — regardless of
#   where it sits in the tree. None of it may be published.
#
#   The rule is enforced, not just documented: .githooks/pre-commit rejects any
#   commit that stages a data path or an oversized blob. Enable it once per
#   clone with:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# UNITY RULE OF THUMB
#   An asset and its .meta file are one unit. Ignore both together or track both
#   together — never one without the other, or Unity churns GUIDs on every
#   machine and you get phantom add/delete diffs.
# =============================================================================


# =========================
# DATA — NEVER TRACKED, NEVER PUBLISHED
# =========================
# No leading slash: these match at any depth, including inside Unity/.
Raw_data/
Processed_data/

# Geospatial / point-cloud / mesh payloads, wherever they land.
*.laz
*.las
*.copc.laz
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.sbn
*.sbx
*.qix
*.tif
*.tiff
*.tfw
*.trj
*.ply
*.glb
*.gltf
*.fbx
*.parquet
*.npy
*.pkl

# ...and the Unity .meta twins of those payloads, so Assets/ never ends up with
# a tracked .meta pointing at an untracked asset (see UNITY RULE OF THUMB).
*.laz.meta
*.las.meta
*.gpkg.meta
*.tif.meta
*.tiff.meta
*.ply.meta
*.glb.meta
*.gltf.meta
*.fbx.meta


# =========================
# PYTHON
# =========================
venv/
.venv/
conda_env/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/


# =========================
# UNITY — GENERATED / DERIVED PROJECT FOLDERS
# =========================
# Ignore Unity's generated folders, NOT the whole project: Assets/Scripts/ holds
# real authored source (PLY importer, georeferenced city loader) and
# ProjectSettings/ + Packages/ are what make a clone open identically.
Unity/*/[Ll]ibrary/
Unity/*/[Tt]emp/
Unity/*/[Oo]bj/
Unity/*/[Bb]uild/
Unity/*/[Bb]uilds/
Unity/*/[Ll]ogs/
Unity/*/UserSettings/
Unity/*/MemoryCaptures/
Unity/*/[Rr]ecordings/
Unity/*/Bee/
Unity/*/artifacts/
Unity/*/.vsconfig

# Unity 6 / package-generated caches inside Assets.
Unity/*/Assets/AssetStoreTools*
Unity/*/Assets/StreamingAssets/aa/
Unity/*/Assets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*
Unity/*/Assets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*

# Editor UI state that Unity writes on first use of the Scene Template window.
# Not needed to open or build the project; it only churns. Track it instead if
# the project ever ships real scene templates.
Unity/*/ProjectSettings/SceneTemplateSettings.json

# Build products and crash/diagnostic droppings.
*.unitypackage
*.apk
*.aab
*.app
*.exe
*.pdb
*.mdb
sysinfo.txt
crashlytics-build.properties

# -------------------------
# Generated city geometry (the big one)
# -------------------------
# The city loader builds meshes at edit time from Processed_data/. If that
# scene is saved, Unity serializes every vertex into the .unity YAML — the
# working SampleScene.unity hit 220 MB this way, against 11 KB clean.
#
# SampleScene.unity is tracked ONLY as the clean template: camera, light, and
# the CityMeshLoader component. Load the city, then "Save As" into Generated/
# below if you want to keep it locally. Never save the city into the template.
Unity/*/Assets/Scenes/Generated/
Unity/*/Assets/Scenes/Generated.meta

# Baked lighting is derived output, not source.
Unity/*/Assets/Scenes/*/Lightmap-*
Unity/*/Assets/Scenes/*/ReflectionProbe-*
Unity/*/Assets/**/LightingData.asset
Unity/*/Assets/**/LightingData.asset.meta


# =========================
# IDE / EDITOR
# =========================
# Unity regenerates all of these from the .asmdef files on open.
*.csproj
*.sln
*.slnx
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.vsconfig
.vs/
.idea/

# Keep only the shared VS Code settings, not per-user state.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json


# =========================
# OS
# =========================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# =========================
# GENERATED / DERIVED ARTIFACTS
# =========================
graphify-out/
validation_output.txt
